      "code": "",
      "note": "When the subscriber being individually drained is the head of drainableSubscribers, the code sets drainableSubscribers to nullptr instead of s->next. This orphans all subsequent subscribers in the doubly-linked list: they retain numMessageIndices > 0 and stale messageIndices but are unreachable from the list head. The same bug exists in freeSubscriber at line 233. The patch introduces unlinkDrainableSubscriber() that correctly sets drainableSubscribers to s->next.",
